.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_DUMP_HDL 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_dump_hdl
.Nd print internal nexus event-handle diagnostics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_event_dump_hdl
.Fa "struct ndi_event_hdl *hdl"
.Fa "char *location"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va hdl
Internal event handle to inspect.
.It Va location
Null-terminated label included in diagnostic messages.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_event_dump_hdl()\fP prints the owning node, event counts, cookies,
definitions, and callback registrations associated with \fBhdl\fP through
\fBcmn_err()\fP.
The string \fBlocation\fP labels the diagnostic output.
.Pp
This is an event-framework debugging routine declared only when \fBDEBUG\fP is
defined.
The caller must own the handle's internal \fBndi_evthdl_mutex\fP and ensure
that the callback lists remain stable while they are inspected.
Ordinary nexus drivers should use the opaque-handle interfaces instead of
depending on the internal layout or this debugging entry point.
.Sh CONTEXT
Use in event-framework debugging paths with the required internal
lock held.
The output routine must be usable at the current priority.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
This function has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmn_err 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_alloc_hdl 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
